LeetCode 21 — Merge Two Sorted Lists
Problem Understanding

You are given two sorted linked lists:

list1 = 1 → 2 → 4
list2 = 1 → 3 → 4

Merge them into one sorted linked list:

1 → 1 → 2 → 3 → 4 → 4

Important:

Both lists are already sorted.
We should preserve sorted order.
We can reuse the existing nodes instead of creating new nodes.

Approach 1 — Brute Force: Store Values + Sort
Idea

The simplest approach is:

Traverse list1 and store all values.
Traverse list2 and store all values.
Sort the combined array.
Create a new linked list.

This ignores the fact that the input lists are already sorted, so it is not optimal.

Code
class Solution {
    public ListNode mergeTwoLists(ListNode list1, ListNode list2) {

        ArrayList<Integer> arr = new ArrayList<>();

        while (list1 != null) {
            arr.add(list1.val);
            list1 = list1.next;
        }

        while (list2 != null) {
            arr.add(list2.val);
            list2 = list2.next;
        }

        Collections.sort(arr);

        ListNode dummy = new ListNode(0);
        ListNode curr = dummy;

        for (int value : arr) {
            curr.next = new ListNode(value);
            curr = curr.next;
        }

        return dummy.next;
    }
}

Dry Run

Input:

list1 = 1 → 2 → 4
list2 = 1 → 3 → 4

